package CanvasNet {
    part def SvgCodec {
        doc /* Decode/rasterize-only loader for a common real-world subset of SVG documents, rasterizing them into Surface pixel buffers. The codec itself performs no file or network I/O: an image element's external href is loaded only through the explicit, opt-in SvgLoadOptions.ImageResolver (an IImageResolver of the core ImageSources subsystem), whose calls are charged against the shared work budget and whose pictures are never cached; a data URI is decoded by the codec itself. Every SVG length accepts CSS units (px, pt, pc, in, cm, mm, Q, em, ex, ch, rem, lh, rlh, vw, vh, vmin, vmax), percentages and calc()/min()/max()/clamp(), resolved to user units by one shared resolver (SvgCodec.Lengths.cs) under a three-class malformed-value policy (strict for geometry, tolerant for the root size and paint servers, ignored for font properties); font-size, line-height and the font shorthand are resolved in SvgCodec.FontSize.cs. The SvgImageSource unit-level class is the IImageSource for .svg files: it draws a linked SVG file at the size of its placement over a transparent background and resolves that file's own images through the scoped resolver of the request. An internal (non-public) RenderDiagnostics/LoadWithDiagnostics seam lets tests observe rendering decisions without changing the public API. Position bindings (attributes in the namespace https://demaconsulting.com/canvasnet: x1y1 and x2y2 on a line, center on a circle or an ellipse, xy on a text, valued #imageId selector) are resolved by a pre-pass before painting (SvgCodec.Bindings.cs): each bound image is loaded once through IImagePositionResolver at the device size the painter requests and that same surface is painted, the single matching position is mapped through the painter's placement and the inverse of the element's transforms, and the numbers are written into the element; a binding that fails keeps the written numbers and is reported with a stable svg-binding code through SvgLoadOptions.BindingHandler as an SvgPositionBinding. A closepath is a real segment for markers, as in SVG 2: a closed subpath gets a closing vertex at its first point, so the marker-end of a closed path or a polygon is drawn there, oriented by bisecting the closing and the first segment. Marker content is clipped to its markerWidth by markerHeight viewport unless the marker's overflow is visible or auto, as in browsers. When SvgLoadOptions.HintHandler is set, the codec reports authoring hints as SvgHint records after painting (SvgCodec.Hints.cs), at most once per code per document with a count: svg-arrowhead-shape for a filled triangle or notched head drawn by hand on an unmarked end of a stroked connector, ignoring templates, marker, pattern, mask, and clip-path content, and content drawn through use; a hint never changes the pixels or fails the render. A text is laid out as styled, positioned runs (SvgCodec.TextLayout.cs), shared by painting, the filter bounds pre-pass and clip-path text: tspan and a take their own cascade, x/y/dx/dy lists place characters, an absolute position starts a text chunk anchored by the text-anchor of its first character, baseline-shift moves a run, and white space collapses as in browsers; a is drawn like a group and switch draws its first child that does not need foreignObject. When SvgLoadOptions.UnsupportedFeatureHandler is set, the codec reports SvgUnsupportedFeature records after painting (SvgCodec.Unsupported.cs), at most once per code with a count: svg-text-not-drawn for text it does not draw, and svg-text-unsupported for text drawn without a feature it uses (filters draw primitiveUnits and primitive subregions as specified, so svg-filter-unsupported is no longer reported); a report never changes the pixels or fails the render, and SvgImageSource returns the reports of a linked file as Unsupported notes, or throws UnsupportedImageFeatureException when the request asks to. */

        comment sourceRef /* Source: src/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.Svg/SvgCodec.cs, src/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.Svg/SvgCodec.Core.cs, src/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.Svg/SvgCodec.Parsing.cs, src/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.Svg/SvgCodec.Elements.cs, src/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.Svg/SvgCodec.Shapes.cs, src/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.Svg/SvgCodec.PathData.cs, src/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.Svg/SvgCodec.PathRender.cs, src/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.Svg/SvgCodec.Filters.cs, src/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.Svg/SvgCodec.Filters.ColorMatrix.cs, src/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.Svg/SvgCodec.Filters.ComponentTransfer.cs, src/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.Svg/SvgCodec.Filters.Morphology.cs, src/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.Svg/SvgCodec.Filters.Convolution.cs, src/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.Svg/SvgCodec.Filters.DisplacementMap.cs, src/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.Svg/SvgCodec.Filters.Tile.cs, src/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.Svg/SvgCodec.Filters.DropShadow.cs, src/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.Svg/SvgCodec.Filters.FeImage.cs, src/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.Svg/SvgCodec.Paint.cs, src/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.Svg/SvgCodec.Gradients.cs, src/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.Svg/SvgCodec.Markers.cs, src/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.Svg/SvgCodec.Text.cs, src/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.Svg/SvgCodec.Attributes.cs, src/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.Svg/SvgCodec.Lengths.cs, src/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.Svg/SvgCodec.FontSize.cs, src/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.Svg/SvgFontFace.cs, src/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.Svg/SvgFontStyle.cs, src/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.Svg/SvgLoadOptions.cs, src/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.Svg/SvgImageSource.cs, src/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.Svg/SvgCodec.Fonts.cs, src/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.Svg/SvgCodec.ClippingAndMasking.cs, src/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.Svg/SvgCodec.Patterns.cs, src/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.Svg/SvgCodec.PreserveAspectRatio.cs, src/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.Svg/SvgCodec.Image.cs, src/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.Svg/SvgCodec.Filters.Lighting.cs, src/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.Svg/SvgCodec.Filters.Turbulence.cs, src/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.Svg/SvgCodec.Filters.Blend.cs, src/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.Svg/SvgCodec.Css.Parser.cs, src/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.Svg/SvgCodec.Css.Selectors.cs, src/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.Svg/SvgCodec.Css.Cascade.cs, src/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet/Codecs/ImageInfo.cs (cross-package: shared header-only probe result type in the core DemaConsulting.CanvasNet package), src/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.Svg/SvgCodec.Bindings.cs, src/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.Svg/SvgPositionBinding.cs, src/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.Svg/SvgCodec.Hints.cs, src/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.Svg/SvgHint.cs, src/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.Svg/SvgCodec.TextLayout.cs, src/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.Svg/SvgCodec.Unsupported.cs, src/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.Svg/SvgUnsupportedFeature.cs */
        comment testRef /* Test: test/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.Svg.Tests/SvgCodecTests.cs, test/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.Svg.Tests/SvgFixtureTests.cs, test/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.Svg.Tests/SvgSystemIntegrationTests.cs, test/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.Svg.Tests/SvgImageResamplingTests.cs, test/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.Svg.Tests/SvgImageResolverTests.cs, test/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.Svg.Tests/SvgImageSourceTests.cs, test/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.Svg.Tests/SvgPatternTileSmoothingTests.cs, test/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.Svg.Tests/SvgDefaultFontTests.cs, test/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.Svg.Tests/SvgLengthUnitTests.cs, test/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.Svg.Tests/SvgFontSizeTests.cs, test/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.Svg.Tests/SvgLengthTestSupport.cs, test/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.Svg.Tests/SvgPositionBindingTests.cs, test/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.Svg.Tests/SvgArrowTests.cs, test/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.Svg.Tests/SvgTextLayoutTests.cs, test/DemaConsulting.CanvasNet.Svg.Tests/SvgUnsupportedFeatureTests.cs */
        comment designRef /* Design: docs/design/canvas-net-svg/svg-codec.md */
        comment verificationRef /* Verification: docs/verification/canvas-net-svg/svg-codec.md */
        comment reqRef /* Requirements: docs/reqstream/canvas-net-svg/svg-codec.yaml */
    }
